 "evaluation": "All three responses properly recognize this as a genuine conflict between two observational studies of vitamin D status and depression. Response A is the strongest because it selects `design_or_bias` as the primary reason (cross-sectional online survey with self-reported deficiency vs. cohort study with objectively measured serum vitamin D levels) and includes `population`, `intervention` (exposure definition), and `outcome_measure` in `also_differs`. Responses B and C choose `population` as the primary reason, which is also very defensible (general US adults vs. at-risk pregnant women), with C slightly ahead of B for explicitly noting the exposure and sample size differences in its detail.",
